  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed retention of the vehicle repair and maintenance use within Arches 75 and 76 would expand the principal repair operation from the two arches authorised under planning permission 031349 to all four arches forming the wider planning unit. Having regard to the close proximity of residential properties and the noise, vehicle movements, fumes, odours, customer activity and general disturbance associated with the operation, the development would result in a scale and intensity of activity incompatible with the surrounding residential context and harmful to the living conditions of neighbouring occupiers. The application is not supported by sufficient acoustic, environmental or operational evidence demonstrating that these impacts can be satisfactorily controlled. The proposal is therefore contrary to Policies 1, 34, 50 and 57 of the Waltham Forest Local Plan Part 1 (2024) and Policy D14 of the London Plan (2021).",
    "The development fails to provide a safe and satisfactory arrangement for vehicle access, parking, manoeuvring, servicing and the storage of vehicles associated with the business. The operation gives rise to parking overspill within residents’ parking bays, parking on waiting restrictions and footways, vehicle movements across the public footway and conflict with pedestrians, cyclists and other highway users. Furthermore, the submitted plans fail to illustrate the existing third vehicle access, which does not align with an authorised vehicle crossover, and no Transport Assessment, access strategy, parking management plan or satisfactory mitigation scheme has been provided. The proposal would therefore prejudice highway safety and the safe and convenient operation of the public highway, contrary to Policies 34, 63 and 64 of the Waltham Forest Local Plan Part 1 (2024)."
  ],
